@startuml
title UC-01 - Create Application and set Environment Connection once
autonumber
actor Developer as Dev
boundary ApplicationController as API
control ApplicationService as Service
control "ApplicationService.SetConnection" as Target
database ApplicationRepository as Apps
database EnvironmentRepository as Envs
database ConnectionRepository as Connections
database DeploymentSetRepository as Sets
Dev -> API: CreateApplication(name, subdomain)
API -> Service: Validate and generate Application ID
Service -> Apps: Save identity/provider <<transaction>>
Service -> Envs: Save staging/production UNCONFIGURED <<transaction>>
Service -> Sets: Save empty Sets/current pointers <<transaction>>
Service --> Dev: Application with independent unset targets
Dev -> API: Open selected Environment Settings
API -> Connections: List session Organization READY supported choices
Connections --> Dev: safe choices; default marker only
Dev -> API: SetConnection(app, env, key, expectedVersion)
API -> Target: SetConnection(session Organization, command)
Target -> Envs: Check scoped ownership, unset binding/version <<transaction>>
Target -> Connections: Validate READY kind/region in Organization <<transaction>>
Target -> Envs: CAS unset target, bump version, freeze binding <<transaction>>
Envs --> Target: configured Environment or conflict
Target --> Dev: read-only target; other Environment unchanged
note over Target,Envs
Any second set is 409, including same key.
No external provisioning; no default fallback.
end note
@enduml
